  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931806/assets/4f7a6bc26eab91db2abe7890075db6fe8fd7e632282b680fe1907156830bbbc3.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}+c.$ What is the value of $c?$",
  "worked_solution": "The horizontal asymptote of $y={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}$ is $y=0.$\n\nThe vertical translation $y={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=2.$ Therefore, $c=2.$",
